IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc11-definitions`

-- ccc11-evidence.l4 -- Part VIII.1, sections 320.31 to 320.35 (Evidentiary Matters: breath and blood results, presumptions, admissibility, certificates, disclosure, the presumption of operation)
-- of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46. LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- A rule of evidence ("is admissible", "is evidence of", "is presumed") answers JUST TRUE when its stated conditions hold; JUST FALSE where the text's own "if", "unless" or "in the absence of evidence to the contrary"
-- is unmet or defeats it, or where a period the text fixes in its own words has not run; NOTHING where the text does not speak. A period of days is counted with `Day` (the day number), so "at least 30 days before"
-- is a difference of at least 30. Numbers the text leaves to a regulation or to a sample (concentrations, results) are inputs.

-- Line 6413: the division heading "Evidentiary Matters": inert (reason 1, a heading).
-- src:6413 | Evidentiary Matters
§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.31: breath samples, blood samples, presumptions and admissibility`

-- (1): "If samples of a person's breath have been received into an approved instrument operated by a qualified technician, the results of the analyses of the samples are conclusive proof of the person's blood alcohol
-- concentration at the time when the analyses were made if the results of the analyses are the same -- or, if different, the lowest of the results is conclusive proof -- if (a) before each sample was taken, the qualified
-- technician conducted a system blank test the result of which is not more than 10 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood and a system calibration check the result of which is within 10% of the target value of an alcohol standard
-- that is certified by an analyst; (b) there was an interval of at least 15 minutes between the times when the samples were taken; and (c) the results of the analyses, rounded down to the nearest multiple of 10 mg, did not
-- differ by more than 20 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood." Two samples are modelled (the text says "the samples"); with more, the rule is applied to the first two.
-- src:6414 | Breath samples
-- src:6415 | 320.31 (1) If samples of a person’s breath have been received into an approved instrument operated by a qualified technician, the results of the analyses of the samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration at the time when the analyses were made if the results of the analyses are the same — or, if the results of the analyses are different, the lowest of the results is conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration at the time when the analyses were made — if
-- src:6416 | (a) before each sample was taken, the qualified technician conducted a system blank test the result of which is not more than 10 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood and a system calibration check the result of which is within 10% of the target value of an alcohol standard that is certified by an analyst;
-- src:6417 | (b) there was an interval of at least 15 minutes between the times when the samples were taken; and
-- src:6418 | (c) the results of the analyses, rounded down to the nearest multiple of 10 mg, did not differ by more than 20 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(1) (src:6414-6418)
GIVEN `the samples of the person’s breath were received into an approved instrument, by s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the instrument was operated by a qualified technician, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result of the system blank test conducted before each sample was taken, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER
      `the result of the system calibration check conducted before each sample was taken, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER
      `the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER
      `the alcohol standard is certified by an analyst, by s 320.11 the person is an analyst` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the interval between the times when the samples were taken, in minutes` IS A NUMBER
      `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER
      `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` MEANS
    IF `the result of the system blank test conducted before each sample was taken, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` GREATER THAN 10
       OR `the result of the system calibration check conducted before each sample was taken, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` LESS THAN `the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` MINUS (`the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` TIMES 0.1)
       OR `the result of the system calibration check conducted before each sample was taken, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` GREATER THAN `the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` PLUS (`the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` TIMES 0.1)
       OR `the interval between the times when the samples were taken, in minutes` LESS THAN 15
       OR (rounded `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` MINUS rounded `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood`) GREATER THAN 20
       OR (rounded `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` MINUS rounded `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood`) GREATER THAN 20
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) before each sample was taken, the qualified technician conducted a system blank test the result of which is not more than 10 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood and a system calibration check the result of which is within 10% of the target value of an alcohol standard that is certified by an analyst; (b) there was an interval of at least 15 minutes between the times when the samples were taken; and (c) the results of the analyses, rounded down to the nearest multiple of 10 mg, did not differ by more than 20 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood" (an "if" condition unmet)
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: both hold`
             (`s 320.11 helper: both hold` `the samples of the person’s breath were received into an approved instrument, by s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` `the instrument was operated by a qualified technician, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples`)
             `the alcohol standard is certified by an analyst, by s 320.11 the person is an analyst`
    WHERE
        rounded x MEANS FLOOR (x DIVIDED BY 10) TIMES 10
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- The concentration the results prove: "the results of the analyses are the same -- or, if the results of the analyses are different, the lowest of the results". Where the conditions of the subsection are not met
-- this subsection does not make the results conclusive proof of anything: NOT COVERED.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(1) (src:6414-6418)
GIVEN `the conditions of subsection 320.31(1) are met, by s 320.31(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER
      `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 320.31(1) the blood alcohol concentration that the results are conclusive proof of, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` MEANS
    IF `the conditions of subsection 320.31(1) are met, by s 320.31(1)` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST (IF `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` AT MOST `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` THEN `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` ELSE `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the results of the analyses of the samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration at the time when the analyses were made if the results of the analyses are the same"

-- (2): "The result of an analysis made by an analyst of a sample of a person's blood is proof of their blood alcohol concentration or their blood drug concentration, as the case may be, at the time when the sample was taken in the
-- absence of evidence tending to show that the analysis was performed improperly." The proof gives way to such evidence ("in the absence of": JUST FALSE where there is some).
-- src:6419 | Blood samples — concentration when sample taken
-- src:6420 | (2) The result of an analysis made by an analyst of a sample of a person’s blood is proof of their blood alcohol concentration or their blood drug concentration, as the case may be, at the time when the sample was taken in the absence of evidence tending to show that the analysis was performed improperly.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(2) (src:6419-6420)
GIVEN `the analysis was made by an analyst, by s 320.11 the person is an analyst` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence tending to show that the analysis was performed improperly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(2) the result of the analysis of the blood sample is proof of the person’s concentration at the time the sample was taken` MEANS
    IF `there is evidence tending to show that the analysis was performed improperly`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is proof of their blood alcohol concentration or their blood drug concentration, as the case may be, at the time when the sample was taken in the absence of evidence tending to show that the analysis was performed improperly"
    ELSE `the analysis was made by an analyst, by s 320.11 the person is an analyst`

-- (3): "Evidence of the following does not constitute evidence tending to show that an analysis of a sample of a person's blood was performed improperly: (a) the amount of alcohol or a drug that they consumed; (b) the rate at which ...
-- absorbed or eliminated; or (c) a calculation based on the evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b)." A flat negative for those three kinds of evidence; any other kind of evidence is not addressed.
DECLARE `s 320.31(3) kind of evidence` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.31(3)(a) evidence of the amount of alcohol or a drug that they consumed`
    `s 320.31(3)(b) evidence of the rate at which the alcohol or the drug would have been absorbed or eliminated by their body`
    `s 320.31(3)(c) a calculation based on the evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of what their blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration would have been at the time the sample was taken`
    `s 320.31(3) evidence of any other kind`

-- src:6421 | Evidence not included
-- src:6422 | (3) Evidence of the following does not constitute evidence tending to show that an analysis of a sample of a person’s blood was performed improperly:
-- src:6423 | (a) the amount of alcohol or a drug that they consumed;
-- src:6424 | (b) the rate at which the alcohol or the drug would have been absorbed or eliminated by their body; or
-- src:6425 | (c) a calculation based on the evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of what their blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration would have been at the time the sample was taken.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(3) (src:6421-6425)
GIVEN `the evidence` IS A `s 320.31(3) kind of evidence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(3) the evidence constitutes evidence tending to show that the analysis of the blood sample was performed improperly` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the evidence`
    WHEN `s 320.31(3) evidence of any other kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names only the three kinds of evidence in paragraphs (a) to (c)
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not constitute evidence tending to show that an analysis of a sample of a person’s blood was performed improperly"

-- (4): the presumption: "For the purpose of paragraphs 320.14(1)(b) and (d), if the first of the samples of breath was taken, or the sample of blood was taken, more than two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance and the
-- person's blood alcohol concentration was equal to or exceeded 20 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood, the person's blood alcohol concentration within those two hours is conclusively presumed to be the concentration established in
-- accordance with subsection (1) or (2), as the case may be, plus an additional 5 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood for every interval of 30 minutes in excess of those two hours." Reading taken (fork F14): complete intervals of 30 minutes.
-- src:6426 | Presumption — blood alcohol concentration
-- src:6427 | (4) For the purpose of paragraphs 320.14(1)(b) and (d), if the first of the samples of breath was taken, or the sample of blood was taken, more than two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance and the person’s blood alcohol concentration was equal to or exceeded 20 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood, the person’s blood alcohol concentration within those two hours is conclusively presumed to be the concentration established in accordance with subsection (1) or (2), as the case may be, plus an additional 5 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood for every interval of 30 minutes in excess of those two hours.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(4) (src:6426-6427)
GIVEN `the number of minutes after the person ceased to operate the conveyance at which the first of the samples of breath was taken, or the sample of blood was taken` IS A NUMBER
      `the blood alcohol concentration established in accordance with subsection 320.31(1) or (2), in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` MEANS
    IF `the number of minutes after the person ceased to operate the conveyance at which the first of the samples of breath was taken, or the sample of blood was taken` GREATER THAN 120
       AND `the blood alcohol concentration established in accordance with subsection 320.31(1) or (2), in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` AT LEAST 20
    THEN JUST (`the blood alcohol concentration established in accordance with subsection 320.31(1) or (2), in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` PLUS 5 TIMES (FLOOR ((`the number of minutes after the person ceased to operate the conveyance at which the first of the samples of breath was taken, or the sample of blood was taken` MINUS 120) DIVIDED BY 30)))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the first of the samples of breath was taken, or the sample of blood was taken, more than two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance and the person’s blood alcohol concentration was equal to or exceeded 20 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood"

-- (5): "An evaluating officer's opinion relating to the impairment, by a type of drug that they identified, or by a combination of alcohol and that type of drug, of a person's ability to operate a conveyance is admissible in
-- evidence without qualifying the evaluating officer as an expert."
-- src:6428 | Admissibility of evaluating officer’s opinion
-- src:6429 | (5) An evaluating officer’s opinion relating to the impairment, by a type of drug that they identified, or by a combination of alcohol and that type of drug, of a person’s ability to operate a conveyance is admissible in evidence without qualifying the evaluating officer as an expert.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(5) (src:6428-6429)
GIVEN `the opinion is that of an evaluating officer, by s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the opinion relates to the impairment, by a type of drug that they identified, or by a combination of alcohol and that type of drug, of a person’s ability to operate a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(5) the evaluating officer’s opinion is admissible in evidence without qualifying the evaluating officer as an expert` MEANS
    IF `the opinion relates to the impairment, by a type of drug that they identified, or by a combination of alcohol and that type of drug, of a person’s ability to operate a conveyance` AND `the opinion is that of an evaluating officer, by s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An evaluating officer’s opinion relating to the impairment, by a type of drug that they identified, or by a combination of alcohol and that type of drug, of a person’s ability to operate a conveyance is admissible"

-- (6): "If the analysis of a sample provided under subsection 320.28(4) demonstrates that the person has a drug in their body that is of a type that the evaluating officer has identified as impairing the person's ability to operate a
-- conveyance, that drug -- or, if the person has also consumed alcohol, the combination of alcohol and that drug -- is presumed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, to be the drug ... that was present in the person's body at the
-- time when the person operated the conveyance and, on proof of the person's impairment, to have been the cause of that impairment." Two presumptions.
-- src:6430 | Presumption — drug
-- src:6431 | (6) If the analysis of a sample provided under subsection 320.28(4) demonstrates that the person has a drug in their body that is of a type that the evaluating officer has identified as impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance, that drug — or, if the person has also consumed alcohol, the combination of alcohol and that drug — is presumed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, to be the drug, or the combination of alcohol and that drug, that was present in the person’s body at the time when the person operated the conveyance and, on proof of the person’s impairment, to have been the cause of that impairment.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(6) (src:6430-6431)
GIVEN `the analysis of a sample provided under subsection 320.28(4) demonstrates that the person has a drug in their body that is of a type that the evaluating officer has identified as impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been present in the person’s body at the time when the person operated the conveyance` MEANS
    IF `the analysis of a sample provided under subsection 320.28(4) demonstrates that the person has a drug in their body that is of a type that the evaluating officer has identified as impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance` AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the analysis of a sample provided under subsection 320.28(4) demonstrates that the person has a drug in their body ... is presumed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary" (the "if" unmet, or there is evidence to the contrary)

@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(6) (src:6430-6431)
GIVEN `the analysis of a sample provided under subsection 320.28(4) demonstrates that the person has a drug in their body that is of a type that the evaluating officer has identified as impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person’s impairment is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been the cause of the person’s impairment` MEANS
    IF `the analysis of a sample provided under subsection 320.28(4) demonstrates that the person has a drug in their body that is of a type that the evaluating officer has identified as impairing the person’s ability to operate a conveyance` AND `the person’s impairment is proved` AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on proof of the person’s impairment, to have been the cause of that impairment" (the "if" or the proof unmet, or there is evidence to the contrary)

-- (7): "The result of an analysis of a sample of a person's breath, blood, urine, sweat or other bodily substance that they were not required to provide under this Part may be admitted in evidence even if the person was not warned
-- before they provided the sample that they were not required to do so or that the result of the analysis of the sample might be used in evidence."
-- src:6432 | Admissibility of result of analysis
-- src:6433 | (7) The result of an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath, blood, urine, sweat or other bodily substance that they were not required to provide under this Part may be admitted in evidence even if the person was not warned before they provided the sample that they were not required to do so or that the result of the analysis of the sample might be used in evidence.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(7) (src:6432-6433)
GIVEN `the person was not required to provide the sample under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(7) the result of the analysis may be admitted in evidence even if the person was not warned` MEANS
    IF `the person was not required to provide the sample under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a sample of a person’s breath, blood, urine, sweat or other bodily substance that they were not required to provide under this Part"

-- (8): "Unless a person is required to provide a sample of a bodily substance under this Part, evidence that they failed or refused to provide a sample for analysis or that a sample was not taken is not admissible and the failure,
-- refusal or fact that a sample was not taken shall not be the subject of comment by any person in any proceedings under this Part." Where the person was required, the "unless" is met and the subsection says nothing (NOT COVERED:
-- the admissibility of the failure to comply with a demand is subsection (10)'s; fork F15).
-- src:6434 | Evidence of failure to provide sample
-- src:6435 | (8) Unless a person is required to provide a sample of a bodily substance under this Part, evidence that they failed or refused to provide a sample for analysis or that a sample was not taken is not admissible and the failure, refusal or fact that a sample was not taken shall not be the subject of comment by any person in any proceedings under this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(8) (src:6434-6435)
GIVEN `the person is required to provide a sample of a bodily substance under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(8) evidence that the person failed or refused to provide a sample, or that a sample was not taken, is not admissible` MEANS
    IF `the person is required to provide a sample of a bodily substance under this Part`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the "unless" is met and the subsection then says nothing about admissibility
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(8) (src:6434-6435)
GIVEN `the person is required to provide a sample of a bodily substance under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(8) the failure, refusal or fact that a sample was not taken shall not be the subject of comment by any person in any proceedings under this Part` MEANS
    IF `the person is required to provide a sample of a bodily substance under this Part`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the "unless" is met and the subsection then says nothing about comment
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (9): "A statement made by a person to a peace officer, including a statement compelled under a provincial Act, is admissible in evidence for the purpose of justifying a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28."
-- src:6436 | Admissibility of statement
-- src:6437 | (9) A statement made by a person to a peace officer, including a statement compelled under a provincial Act, is admissible in evidence for the purpose of justifying a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(9) (src:6436-6437)
GIVEN `the statement was made to a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement is offered for the purpose of justifying a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(9) the statement is admissible in evidence for the purpose of justifying a demand` MEANS
    IF `the statement is offered for the purpose of justifying a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28` AND `the statement was made to a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A statement made by a person to a peace officer ... is admissible in evidence for the purpose of justifying a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28"

-- (10): "In any proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14, evidence that the accused, without reasonable excuse, failed or refused to comply with a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28 is admissible and the
-- court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from that evidence." Two answers: the evidence is admissible (not named for a power: NOTHING outside its stated conditions); the court may draw the inference (a power
-- whose gate is "In any proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14", of the "in the case of" kind: listed, not flipped, fork F36 in NOTES.md, so outside such proceedings the answer is the guide's JUST FALSE).
-- src:6438 | Evidence of failure to comply with demand
-- src:6439 | (10) In any proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14, evidence that the accused, without reasonable excuse, failed or refused to comply with a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28 is admissible and the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from that evidence.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(10) (src:6438-6439)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is that the accused, without reasonable excuse, failed or refused to comply with a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(10) the evidence of the failure or refusal to comply with the demand is admissible` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14` AND `the evidence is that the accused, without reasonable excuse, failed or refused to comply with a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14, evidence that the accused, without reasonable excuse, failed or refused to comply with a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28 is admissible"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.31(10) (src:6438-6439)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is that the accused, without reasonable excuse, failed or refused to comply with a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.31(10) the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the evidence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In any proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14, evidence that the accused, without reasonable excuse, failed or refused to comply with a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28 is admissible and the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused" (an "in any proceedings in respect of" gate: listed, F36; the other reading is NOTHING)
    ELSE IF `the evidence is that the accused, without reasonable excuse, failed or refused to comply with a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from that evidence"

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.32: certificates`

-- (1): "A certificate of an analyst, qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician made under this Part is evidence of the facts alleged in the certificate without proof of the signature or the official character of the person who signed the certificate."
-- src:6440 | Certificates
-- src:6441 | 320.32 (1) A certificate of an analyst, qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician made under this Part is evidence of the facts alleged in the certificate without proof of the signature or the official character of the person who signed the certificate.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.32(1) (src:6440-6441)
GIVEN `the certificate is a certificate of an analyst, qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.32(1) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or the official character of the person who signed it` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is a certificate of an analyst, qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician made under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A certificate of an analyst, qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician made under this Part is evidence of the facts alleged in the certificate"

-- (2): "No certificate shall be received in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given to the other party reasonable notice of their intention to produce it and a copy of the certificate."
-- Asks whether this subsection bars receipt: JUST TRUE (barred) when either was not given; JUST FALSE (not barred by this subsection) when both were.
-- src:6442 | Notice of intention to produce certificate
-- src:6443 | (2) No certificate shall be received in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given to the other party reasonable notice of their intention to produce it and a copy of the certificate.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.32(2) (src:6442-6443)
GIVEN `the party intending to produce the certificate gave the other party, before the trial, reasonable notice of their intention to produce it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party intending to produce the certificate gave the other party, before the trial, a copy of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.32(2) the certificate is barred from being received in evidence` MEANS
    IF `the party intending to produce the certificate gave the other party, before the trial, reasonable notice of their intention to produce it` AND `the party intending to produce the certificate gave the other party, before the trial, a copy of the certificate`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No certificate shall be received in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given to the other party reasonable notice of their intention to produce it and a copy of the certificate" (the "unless" met: this subsection does not bar it)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3): "A party against whom the certificate is produced may apply to the court for an order requiring the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination."
-- src:6444 | Attendance and cross-examination
-- src:6445 | (3) A party against whom the certificate is produced may apply to the court for an order requiring the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.32(3) (src:6444-6445)
GIVEN `the person is a party against whom the certificate is produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.32(3) the party may apply to the court for an order requiring the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for cross-examination` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party against whom the certificate is produced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A party against whom the certificate is produced may apply to the court"

-- (4): "The application shall be made in writing and set out the likely relevance of the proposed cross-examination with respect to the facts alleged in the certificate. A copy of the application shall be given to the prosecutor
-- at least 30 days before the day on which the application is to be heard." Whether the requirements are met: JUST FALSE where one is not.
-- src:6446 | Form and content of application
-- src:6447 | (4) The application shall be made in writing and set out the likely relevance of the proposed cross-examination with respect to the facts alleged in the certificate. A copy of the application shall be given to the prosecutor at least 30 days before the day on which the application is to be heard.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.32(4) (src:6446-6447)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application sets out the likely relevance of the proposed cross-examination with respect to the facts alleged in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which a copy of the application was given to the prosecutor` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application is to be heard` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.32(4) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in writing` AND `the application sets out the likely relevance of the proposed cross-examination with respect to the facts alleged in the certificate`
       AND Day `the day on which the application is to be heard` MINUS Day `the day on which a copy of the application was given to the prosecutor` AT LEAST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application shall be made in writing and set out the likely relevance of the proposed cross-examination with respect to the facts alleged in the certificate. A copy of the application shall be given to the prosecutor at least 30 days before the day on which the application is to be heard"

-- (5): "The hearing of the application shall be held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held."
-- src:6448 | Time of hearing
-- src:6449 | (5) The hearing of the application shall be held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.32(5) (src:6448-6449)
GIVEN `the day on which the hearing of the application is held` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the trial is to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.32(5) the hearing of the application is held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held` MEANS
    IF Day `the day on which the trial is to be held` MINUS Day `the day on which the hearing of the application is held` AT LEAST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The hearing of the application shall be held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held"

-- (6): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under subsection 320.18(1), the following certificates are evidence of the facts alleged in them without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed them:
-- (a) a certificate ... that the person named in it is prohibited from operating a motor vehicle in the province specified in the certificate, signed by the person who is responsible for the registration of motor vehicles in that
-- province or any person authorized by the responsible person to sign it; and (b) ... a conveyance other than a motor vehicle, signed by the Minister of Transport or any person authorized by him or her to sign it."
-- src:6450 | Certificate admissible in evidence
-- src:6451 | (6) In proceedings in respect of an offence under subsection 320.18(1), the following certificates are evidence of the facts alleged in them without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed them:
-- src:6452 | (a) a certificate setting out with reasonable particularity that the person named in it is prohibited from operating a motor vehicle in the province specified in the certificate, signed by the person who is responsible for the registration of motor vehicles in that province or any person authorized by the responsible person to sign it; and
-- src:6453 | (b) a certificate setting out with reasonable particularity that the person named in it is prohibited from operating a conveyance other than a motor vehicle, signed by the Minister of Transport or any person authorized by him or her to sign it.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.32(6) (src:6450-6453)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under subsection 320.18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets out with reasonable particularity that the person named in it is prohibited from operating a motor vehicle in the province specified in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the person who is responsible for the registration of motor vehicles in that province or any person authorized by the responsible person to sign it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.32(6)(a) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under subsection 320.18(1)` AND `the certificate sets out with reasonable particularity that the person named in it is prohibited from operating a motor vehicle in the province specified in the certificate`
       AND `it is signed by the person who is responsible for the registration of motor vehicles in that province or any person authorized by the responsible person to sign it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under subsection 320.18(1), the following certificates are evidence of the facts alleged in them"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.32(6)(b) (src:6450-6453)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under subsection 320.18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets out with reasonable particularity that the person named in it is prohibited from operating a conveyance other than a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the Minister of Transport or any person authorized by the Minister to sign it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.32(6)(b) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under subsection 320.18(1)` AND `the certificate sets out with reasonable particularity that the person named in it is prohibited from operating a conveyance other than a motor vehicle`
       AND `it is signed by the Minister of Transport or any person authorized by the Minister to sign it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under subsection 320.18(1), the following certificates are evidence of the facts alleged in them"

-- (7): "If it is proved that a prohibition under paragraph 320.18(1)(b) has been imposed on a person and that notice of the prohibition has been mailed to them at their last known address, that person is, beginning on the tenth day
-- after the day on which the notice is mailed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, presumed to have received the notice and to have knowledge of the prohibition, of the date of its commencement and of its duration."
-- A period the text fixes in its own words: before the tenth day after mailing, JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)); day 10 and after, JUST TRUE.
-- src:6454 | Onus
-- src:6455 | (7) If it is proved that a prohibition under paragraph 320.18(1)(b) has been imposed on a person and that notice of the prohibition has been mailed to them at their last known address, that person is, beginning on the tenth day after the day on which the notice is mailed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, presumed to have received the notice and to have knowledge of the prohibition, of the date of its commencement and of its duration.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.32(7) (src:6454-6455)
GIVEN `it is proved that a prohibition under paragraph 320.18(1)(b) has been imposed on the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that notice of the prohibition has been mailed to the person at their last known address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the notice was mailed` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.32(7) the person is presumed to have received the notice and to have knowledge of the prohibition, of the date of its commencement and of its duration` MEANS
    IF `it is proved that a prohibition under paragraph 320.18(1)(b) has been imposed on the person` AND `it is proved that notice of the prohibition has been mailed to the person at their last known address`
       AND Day `the day asked about` MINUS Day `the day on which the notice was mailed` AT LEAST 10
       AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it is proved that a prohibition under paragraph 320.18(1)(b) has been imposed on a person and that notice of the prohibition has been mailed to them at their last known address, that person is, beginning on the tenth day after the day on which the notice is mailed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, presumed"

§ `Part VIII.1 -- sections 320.33 to 320.35: printout, disclosure, presumption of operation`

-- 320.33: "A document that is printed out from an approved instrument and signed by a qualified technician who certifies it to be the printout produced by the approved instrument when it made an analysis of a sample of a person's breath
-- is evidence of the facts alleged in the document without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it."
-- src:6456 | Printout from approved instrument
-- src:6457 | 320.33 A document that is printed out from an approved instrument and signed by a qualified technician who certifies it to be the printout produced by the approved instrument when it made an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath is evidence of the facts alleged in the document without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.33 (src:6456-6457)
GIVEN `the document is printed out from an approved instrument, by s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by a qualified technician, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the technician certifies it to be the printout produced by the approved instrument when it made an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.33 the printout is evidence of the facts alleged in the document without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` MEANS
    IF `the technician certifies it to be the printout produced by the approved instrument when it made an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath` AND `the document is printed out from an approved instrument, by s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
       AND `it is signed by a qualified technician, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document that is printed out from an approved instrument and signed by a qualified technician who certifies it to be the printout ... is evidence of the facts alleged in the document"

-- 320.34(1): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14, the prosecutor shall disclose to the accused, with respect to any samples of breath that the accused provided under section 320.28, information sufficient to
-- determine whether the conditions set out in paragraphs 320.31(1)(a) to (c) have been met, namely: (a) the results of the system blank tests; (b) the results of the system calibration checks; (c) any error or exception messages
-- produced by the approved instrument at the time the samples were taken; (d) the results of the analysis of the accused's breath samples; and (e) a certificate of an analyst stating that the sample of an alcohol standard that is
-- identified in the certificate is suitable for use with an approved instrument." A duty of the prosecutor and the accused's claim: JUST FALSE where its "if" is unmet.
-- src:6458 | Disclosure of information
-- src:6459 | 320.34 (1) In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14, the prosecutor shall disclose to the accused, with respect to any samples of breath that the accused provided under section 320.28, information sufficient to determine whether the conditions set out in paragraphs 320.31(1)(a) to (c) have been met, namely:
-- src:6460 | (a) the results of the system blank tests;
-- src:6461 | (b) the results of the system calibration checks;
-- src:6462 | (c) any error or exception messages produced by the approved instrument at the time the samples were taken;
-- src:6463 | (d) the results of the analysis of the accused’s breath samples; and
-- src:6464 | (e) a certificate of an analyst stating that the sample of an alcohol standard that is identified in the certificate is suitable for use with an approved instrument.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.34(1) (src:6458-6464)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused provided samples of breath under section 320.28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.34(1) the prosecutor shall disclose to the accused information about the breath samples` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14` AND `the accused provided samples of breath under section 320.28`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14, the prosecutor shall disclose to the accused, with respect to any samples of breath that the accused provided under section 320.28" (the "if" unmet)

@ref Criminal Code s 320.34(1)(a) to (e) (src:6458-6464)
GIVEN `the prosecutor shall disclose, by s 320.34(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`s 320.34(1)(a) to (e) the information the prosecutor shall disclose` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor shall disclose, by s 320.34(1)` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST (LIST
        "(a) the results of the system blank tests",
        "(b) the results of the system calibration checks",
        "(c) any error or exception messages produced by the approved instrument at the time the samples were taken",
        "(d) the results of the analysis of the accused’s breath samples",
        "(e) a certificate of an analyst stating that the sample of an alcohol standard that is identified in the certificate is suitable for use with an approved instrument")
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14, the prosecutor shall disclose"

DECLARE `s 320.34(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.34(1) disclose to the accused information sufficient to determine whether the conditions set out in paragraphs 320.31(1)(a) to (c) have been met`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.34(1) (src:6458-6464)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused provided samples of breath under section 320.28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320.34(1) action`
`s 320.34(1) the prosecutor shall disclose information about the breath samples to the accused` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14` AND `the accused provided samples of breath under section 320.28`
    THEN PARTY `the prosecutor`
         MUST `s 320.34(1) disclose to the accused information sufficient to determine whether the conditions set out in paragraphs 320.31(1)(a) to (c) have been met`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the prosecutor` BECAUSE "the prosecutor did not disclose the information about the breath samples"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (2): "The accused may apply to the court for a hearing to determine whether further information should be disclosed."
-- src:6465 | Application for further disclosure
-- src:6466 | (2) The accused may apply to the court for a hearing to determine whether further information should be disclosed.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.34(2) (src:6465-6466)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.34(2) the accused may apply to the court for a hearing to determine whether further information should be disclosed` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The accused may apply to the court for a hearing to determine whether further information should be disclosed" (in the proceedings of subsection (1))

-- (3): "The application shall be in writing and set out detailed particulars of the information that the accused seeks to have disclosed and the likely relevance of that information to determining whether the approved instrument was
-- in proper working order. A copy of the application shall be given to the prosecutor at least 30 days before the day on which the application is to be heard."
-- src:6467 | Form and content of application
-- src:6468 | (3) The application shall be in writing and set out detailed particulars of the information that the accused seeks to have disclosed and the likely relevance of that information to determining whether the approved instrument was in proper working order. A copy of the application shall be given to the prosecutor at least 30 days before the day on which the application is to be heard.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.34(3) (src:6467-6468)
GIVEN `the application is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application sets out detailed particulars of the information that the accused seeks to have disclosed and the likely relevance of that information to determining whether the approved instrument was in proper working order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which a copy of the application was given to the prosecutor` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application is to be heard` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.34(3) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` MEANS
    IF `the application is in writing` AND `the application sets out detailed particulars of the information that the accused seeks to have disclosed and the likely relevance of that information to determining whether the approved instrument was in proper working order`
       AND Day `the day on which the application is to be heard` MINUS Day `the day on which a copy of the application was given to the prosecutor` AT LEAST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application shall be in writing and set out detailed particulars of the information that the accused seeks to have disclosed ... A copy of the application shall be given to the prosecutor at least 30 days before the day on which the application is to be heard"

-- (4): "The hearing of the application shall be held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held."
-- src:6469 | Time of hearing
-- src:6470 | (4) The hearing of the application shall be held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.34(4) (src:6469-6470)
GIVEN `the day on which the hearing of the application is held` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the trial is to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.34(4) the hearing of the application is held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held` MEANS
    IF Day `the day on which the trial is to be held` MINUS Day `the day on which the hearing of the application is held` AT LEAST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The hearing of the application shall be held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held"

-- (5): "For greater certainty, nothing in this section limits the disclosure to which the accused may otherwise be entitled." Asks whether this section limits that other disclosure: JUST FALSE where there is one.
-- src:6471 | For greater certainty
-- src:6472 | (5) For greater certainty, nothing in this section limits the disclosure to which the accused may otherwise be entitled.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.34(5) (src:6471-6472)
GIVEN `there is disclosure to which the accused may otherwise be entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.34(5) section 320.34 limits the disclosure to which the accused may otherwise be entitled` MEANS
    IF `there is disclosure to which the accused may otherwise be entitled`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section limits the disclosure to which the accused may otherwise be entitled"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of disclosure to which the accused may otherwise be entitled

-- 320.35: "In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14 or 320.15, if it is proved that the accused occupied the seat or position ordinarily occupied by a person who operates a conveyance, the accused is presumed to
-- have been operating the conveyance unless they establish that they did not occupy that seat or position for the purpose of setting the conveyance in motion."
-- src:6473 | Presumption of operation
-- src:6474 | 320.35 In proceedings in respect of an offence under section 320.14 or 320.15, if it is proved that the accused occupied the seat or position ordinarily occupied by a person who operates a conveyance, the accused is presumed to have been operating the conveyance unless they establish that they did not occupy that seat or position for the purpose of setting the conveyance in motion.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.35 (src:6473-6474)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14 or 320.15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the accused occupied the seat or position ordinarily occupied by a person who operates a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused establishes that they did not occupy that seat or position for the purpose of setting the conveyance in motion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.35 the accused is presumed to have been operating the conveyance` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14 or 320.15` AND `it is proved that the accused occupied the seat or position ordinarily occupied by a person who operates a conveyance`
       AND (NOT `the accused establishes that they did not occupy that seat or position for the purpose of setting the conveyance in motion`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is proved that the accused occupied the seat or position ordinarily occupied by a person who operates a conveyance, the accused is presumed to have been operating the conveyance unless they establish that they did not occupy that seat or position for the purpose of setting the conveyance in motion"
